# Auto merge

Never ask the user for permission to merge — just do it.

After a feature branch PR is ready:

1. Ensure CI on the PR head is green (subscribe and wait; fix failures if needed).
2. Mark draft PRs ready for review when implementation + tests are done.
3. Merge into the preferred base (`main`) with a normal merge commit (`gh pr merge --merge`).
4. If merge conflicts appear after another merge landed first, update the branch from `main`, resolve, push, wait for CI, then merge.
5. Do not force-push `main`/`master`. Do not merge with failing required checks.
6. After merge, briefly confirm; no need to ask whether to merge next time.
